## Comparison purpose and evidence limits

V0–V3 isolate and combine traffic mechanisms; V4 reserves demand, turn-share, bay-storage/length, order and receiving combinations for robustness outside calibration/tuning. The order-only and storage-only cases are separate controls, not a strictly nested information ladder. The printed comparison models use public descriptive names rather than internal codes. The detailed baseline policy and original-series aggregate-inference allowance remain unchanged.

The movement-queue and lane/storage sources remain working model directions, not fully qualified current adapters. Their literature role is now connected to what the ablations should explain. The earlier exclusive-target mixture ablation remains unselected; this revision does not introduce a weaker comparator or select new baseline algorithms.

The new exact arithmetic checks concern the restored overlap grid and its continuous derivative, the explicit entry interval and the rate-to-amount example. Existing reference checks remain historical evidence at their original scope. No simulator, AD/finite-difference traffic experiment, optimization, richer-reference run, package installation or numerical scenario calibration is undertaken. A complete, readable derivative path does not establish implementation correctness or external usefulness.

